{
 "experiment": "b08_security",
 "date": "2026-11-19",
 "method": "Seeded discrete-event runs in the islab twin. Part A: one alarm per run sent by the B01 AlarmHub over the home internet (one_path) or by DualPathAlarmHub over the home internet plus a modelled cellular link (two_paths) to a DualPathCentre that dedupes copies by message and repeats by open incident. Internet down = WanLink outage plus egress gate offline (alarms queue, heartbeats drop). Part B: 24 h with two paths and one alarm of each kind, counting cellular traffic billed. Part C: one week of front camera scenes per seed through an assumed detector model and three designs; household members answer asks through an assumed person model. Ground truth for camera scenes comes from the scene generator, never from messages.",
